'''''Calliandra''''' is a genus of [[flowering plant]]s in the [[pea]] family, [[Fabaceae]], in the [[Mimosoideae|mimosoid clade]] of the subfamily [[Caesalpinioideae]]. It contains about 140 species that are native to [[Tropics|tropical]] and [[Subtropics|subtropical]] regions of the [[Americas]].{{R|DESOUZA}}

==Description==
The genus comprises [[Herbaceous plant|herbaceous]] [[perennial plant]]s, [[shrub]]s, and rarely small [[tree]]s, growing {{convert|0.5|-|6|m|ft|abbr=in|round=0.5}} tall, with [[pinnation|bipinnate]] leaves. The [[flower]]s are produced in cylindrical or globose [[inflorescence]]s and have numerous long slender [[stamen]]s which give rise to the common names '''powder-puff''', '''powder puff plant''', and '''fairy duster'''. These plants flower all year round, but the best blooming is in spring and summer. They can be easily pruned.

Calliandra are often fed on by caterpillars, such as the larvae of statira sulphur (''[[Aphrissa statira]]'').{{R|SRYGLEY}} It is available in many vibrant colours such as pink, white, etc.

